    "result_text": "Typecheck passes cleanly and the e2e test passes. \n\nThe change is complete. Here's what I implemented for **\"When I open a client, show me the projects I am doing for them\"** as a small additive full-stack change:\n\n**Server (OfficeFloor + Spring)**\n- `ProjectRepository.findViewsByClientId(...)` \u2014 a new JPQL query returning one client's projects, oldest first (mirrors the existing `findAllViews`).\n- `ClientProjectsGet.java` \u2014 new logic class for the endpoint.\n- `rest/api/clients/{clientId}/projects.GET.yml` \u2014 new endpoint wiring `GET /api/clients/{clientId}/projects` (under `/api/` so it bypasses the SPA fallback).\n\n**Database** \u2014 no migration needed; `projects.client_id` already exists.\n\n**Front-end (all new files, one small edit)**\n- `routes/clients.tsx` \u2014 one-line `<Outlet/>` layout (the section now has a detail view, per rule 1).\n- `routes/clients.$clientId.tsx` \u2014 the client detail page (child route, not a flag), composing the projects table.\n- `slots/defs/clientRow.ts` \u2014 a new per-row action region on the clients table.\n- `features/clients/open.slot.tsx` \u2014 fills that slot with the `client-open-<id>` link to the detail route.\n- `features/clients/ClientProjectsTable.tsx` \u2014 queries the client's own projects under `['clients', clientId, 'projects']` and renders `client-projects-table`, reusing the `project-row-<id>` / `project-name` anchors.\n- `features/clients/queries.ts` \u2014 added the query key + fetch for a client's projects.\n- `features/clients/ClientsTable.tsx` \u2014 the only edit: added the row-action slot cell (analogous to how `ProjectsTable` already renders `ProjectRow.Slot`).\n\nFeatures stay decoupled (no cross-feature imports); the client detail reuses the projects listing purely through the shared `data-testid` anchors and the `/api/clients/{clientId}/projects` endpoint.",
